WEB SOURCE (THE spec): web/src/components/layout/PageHeaderSticky.tsx
  - A pure presentational scroll affordance. Its only imports are React state (useState/useEffect/
    useCallback) + the lucide `ArrowUp` icon. There is NO data/network layer, hence NO loading / empty /
    error / stale / offline axis. Reproducing those generic template states would be fabrication
    (covenant #5 "no parity shortcuts" / #9 "no silent drift"). The source's REAL render branches are
    reproduced faithfully:
      hidden                 — `if (!visible) return null` → the surface carries no footprint.
      visible · interactive  — `scrollToTop` (default true): the whole bar is a scroll-to-top button
                               with the up-arrow glyph; aria-label = `${ariaLabel} — scroll to top`.
      visible · static       — `scrollToTop={false}`: a labeled, non-interactive `role="region"`.
      (empty content)        — a blank summary resolves to a localized em-dash, never a blank strip.
  - Visibility = the IntersectionObserver guard pair under a `-topOffset` top root-margin:
      `const scrolledPast = entry.boundingClientRect.top < 0;
       setVisible(!entry.isIntersecting && scrolledPast);`
    Native port (PageHeaderStickyVisibility): visible == (heroTop < 0) && (heroBottom <= topOffset).
    The `top < 0` guard is the documented false-positive suppressor for "hero still below the viewport
    on first paint of a long page".
  - Scroll-to-top scrolls the real scroll container (`#main-content`), not window. data-testid →
    accessibilityIdentifier "page-header-sticky".
  - i18n: the web source is "anonymous" — the caller passes an already-localized `ariaLabel`; the only
    English literal is the " — scroll to top" suffix. Per the native no-English-literals rule that
    suffix + the native chrome strings (VoiceOver hint, em-dash, region-label fallback) are promoted to
    the P1/S10 "PageHeaderSticky" table.

DELIVERABLE — apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/PageHeaderSticky.* (the only Allowed source files):
  PageHeaderSticky.swift             Generic surface View: renders nothing while hidden (web `null`),
                                     the interactive/static bar while visible; reduce-motion-respecting
                                     reveal; + a string-summary convenience init.
  PageHeaderSticky.Model.swift       P1/S10 i18n facade (PageHeaderStickyStrings), P1/S11 telemetry seam
                                     (PageHeaderStickyTelemetry + OSLog default), P1/S8 @Observable
                                     state-holder: geometry→visibility, view.opened once on first
                                     reveal, localized a11y labels, host scroll-to-top action.
  PageHeaderSticky.Projection.swift  Pure projections (no SwiftUI): visibility (IntersectionObserver
                                     port), summary em-dash elision, a11y label composition.
  PageHeaderSticky.Views.swift       Bar chrome (translucent material + hairline divider + up-arrow,
                                     tokenized, no ported Tailwind) + PageHeaderStickyScaffold
                                     (ScrollViewReader + onGeometryChange hero tracking + scroll-to-top).
  PageHeaderSticky.Previews.swift    10 previews: interactive / static / long-truncated / empty / top
                                     offset / custom content / scaffold / dark / light / Dynamic Type AX3.
  PageHeaderSticky.Tests.swift       XCTest: visibility projection (incl. false-positive guard + offset
                                     boundary), summary + a11y projections, model (geometry→visibility,
                                     view.opened-exactly-once, activation forward/no-op, topOffset clamp,
                                     stable slug/identifier).
  PageHeaderSticky.strings           P1/S10 catalog contribution (parity suffix + native chrome keys).

